<title>RUSSIA: Russian 1996 gold production estimates.</title>
<headline>Russian 1996 gold production estimates.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-03-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>A Russian Central Bank official put Russia's 1996 gold output at 122 tonnes on Thursday, down from 1995's 135 tonnes, in the third official but different estimate of production for those two years.</p>
<p>The newest preliminary figures were provided by Sergei Kyshtymov, head of the bank's directorate for operations with precious metals, and quoted by Prime Tass news agency.</p>
<p>Following is the range of estimates for gold output, with dates of the forecasts in parentheses:</p>
<p>	  ESTIMATES OF RUSSIAN GOLD PRODUCTION (TONNES)</p>
<p>						1996		 1995</p>
<p>Industry Ministry			 124		  122</p>
<p>(February 21, 1996, quoted</p>
<p>by Prime Tass)</p>
<p>Central Bank				122		  135</p>
<p>(March 20, 1996, quoted by</p>
<p>Prime Tass)</p>
<p> State Statistics Committee	   100.8		108</p>
<p>(1996 annual review, released</p>
<p>end January)</p>
<p>--Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
</text>
